[2m│[0m [1m[38;5;231mWhich change sources should we build now so notifications are actually exercised?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [ ] [38;5;153mCross-tab sync (Recommended)[39m
  [38;5;246mA change in one tab notifies watchers in other open tabs via the storage event. Makes the system demonstrably real [39m
  [38;5;246mwith one user and validates the seam.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m [ ] Due-date arrival (Recommended)
  [38;5;246mA watched task becoming due/overdue generates a notification with no user action — a genuine non-self-caused event.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m [ ] Self-caused changes too
  [38;5;246mNotify even when you made the change yourself in the current tab. Simple and uniform, but this is the redundant-toast
[39m  [38;5;246mcase.[39m
